.SH "NAME"
nvme-sanitize-ns \- Submit a sanitize namespace command
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
.sp
.nf
\fInvme\fR [<global\-options>] \fIsanitize\-ns\fR <device>
                        [\-\-ish | \-I]
                        [\-\-namespace\-id=<num> | \-n <num>]
                        [\-\-ause | \-u]
                        [\-\-sanact=<num> | \-a <num>]
                        [\-\-emvs | \-e]
                        [\-\-preq | \-q]
.fi
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
.sp
Submit a sanitize namespace command\&.
.sp
The <device> parameter is mandatory and may be either the NVMe character device (ex: /dev/nvme0), or a namespace block device (ex: /dev/nvme0n1)\&.
.sp
This page only lists the help texts of the command\&. A detailed description is still missing\&.
.SH "OPTIONS"
.PP
\-I, \-\-ish
.RS 4
Ignore Shutdown (for NVMe\-MI command)
.RE
.PP
\-n <num>, \-\-namespace\-id=<num>
.RS 4
identifier of desired namespace
.sp
Values:
\fIall\fR,
\fI\-1\fR\&.
.RE
.PP
\-u, \-\-ause
.RS 4
Allow unrestricted sanitize exit\&.
.RE
.PP
\-a <num>, \-\-sanact=<num>
.RS 4
Sanitize action: 1 = Exit failure mode,
.sp
.if n \{\
.RS 4
.\}
.nf
4 = Start a crypto erase namespace sanitize operation,
5 = Exit media verification state
.fi
.if n \{\
.RE
.\}
.sp
Values:
\fIexit\-failure\fR,
\fIstart\-crypto\-erase\fR,
\fIexit\-media\-verification\fR\&.
.RE
.PP
\-e, \-\-emvs
.RS 4
Enter media verification state\&.
.RE
.PP
\-q, \-\-preq
.RS 4
Require the sanitize operation to purge user data, as defined by IEEE Std 2883, or fail\&.
.RE
.SH "GLOBAL OPTIONS"
.sp
The following options are defined at the top\-level nvme command and are available to this subcommand:
.PP
\-\-dry\-run
.RS 4
Print the command that would be executed, but do not actually execute it\&.
.RE
.PP
\-\-no\-ioctl\-probing
.RS 4
Disable probing for 64\-bit IOCTL support\&.
.RE
.PP
\-\-no\-retries
.RS 4
Disable retry logic on transient errors\&.
.RE
.PP
\-o <fmt>, \-\-output\-format=<fmt>
.RS 4
Set the reporting format to
\fInormal\fR,
\fItabular, \*(Aqjson\fR, or
\fIbinary\fR\&. Only one output format may be used at a time\&.
.RE
.PP
\-\-output\-format\-version=<version>
.RS 4
Select the output format version\&. Version
\fI1\fR
uses the original field naming, while version
\fI2\fR
(default) provides more consistent and script\-friendly field names\&. Other versions are rejected\&.
.RE
.PP
\-\-quiet
.RS 4
Suppress informational messages\&. Errors are still reported, and \-\-quiet cancels any \-\-verbose for the library log level\&.
.RE
.PP
\-\-set\-options=<key=value>[,<key=value>\&...]
.RS 4
Set libnvme library options for this invocation\&. Supported keys are
\fIforce\-4k\fR,
\fImi\-probe\-enabled\fR,
\fItest\-base\-dir\fR
and
\fItest\-sysfs\-dir\fR\&.
.RE
.PP
\-\-timeout=<ms>
.RS 4
Set the timeout for the command in milliseconds\&.
\fIinfinite\fR
or
\fI\-1\fR
waits without a time limit (0xffffffff)\&.
.RE
.PP
\-v, \-\-verbose
.RS 4
Increase the level of detail in the output\&. May be specified multiple times to further increase verbosity\&.
.RE
.sp
These options can also be set as machine\-wide defaults in nvme\-cli\&.conf(5)\&. A command\-line flag always overrides the file\&.
